title: Bermuda Triangle
text: Count the corners the red beam has to turn, then count your pieces: you are one short. And something must keep the green light out of the triangle.
trick: red enters by the bender at the foot of the triangle, runs round all three sides and comes back into the same bender from above, which turns it a second time out through the corner; six turns from five pieces. The bender at the far corner also takes the green beam on its back
motif: pictogram (a triangular room with a thick hypotenuse, a closet on the diagonal behind the foot, a green light on the far corner)
expect: depth>=3
---
